#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:4
msgid "Ignoring Files"
msgstr "忽略檔案"

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:7
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr "概要"

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:11
msgid ".stignore"
msgstr ".stignore"

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:14
msgid "Description"
msgstr "描述"

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:16
msgid ""
"If some files should not be synchronized to other nodes, a file called ``."
"stignore`` can be created containing file patterns to ignore. The ``."
"stignore`` file must be placed in the root of the repository. The ``."
"stignore`` file itself will never be synced to other nodes, although it can "
"``#include`` files that *are* synchronized between nodes. All patterns are "
"relative to the repository root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:25
msgid ""
"Note that ignored files can block removal of an otherwise empty directory. "
"See below for the (?d) prefix to allow deletion of ignored files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:29
msgid "Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:31
msgid ""
"The ``.stignore`` file contains a list of file or path patterns. The *first* "
"pattern that matches will decide the fate of a given file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:34
msgid ""
"Regular file names match themselves, i.e. the pattern ``foo`` matches the "
"files ``foo``, ``subdir/foo`` as well as any directory named ``foo``. Spaces "
"are treated as regular characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:38
msgid ""
"Asterisk matches zero or more characters in a filename, but does not match "
"the directory separator. ``te*st`` matches ``test``, ``subdir/telerest`` but "
"not ``tele/rest``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:42
msgid ""
"Double asterisk matches as above, but also directory separators. ``te**st`` "
"matches ``test``, ``subdir/telerest`` and ``tele/sub/dir/rest``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:46
msgid ""
"Question mark matches a single character that is not the directory "
"separator. ``te??st`` matches ``tebest`` but not ``teb/st`` or ``test``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:50
msgid ""
"Characters enclosed in square brackets ``[]`` are interpreted as a character "
"range ``[a-z]``. Before using this syntax you should have a basic "
"understanding of regular expression character classes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:52
msgid ""
"A pattern beginning with ``/`` matches in the current directory only. ``/"
"foo`` matches ``foo`` but not ``subdir/foo``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:55
msgid ""
"A pattern beginning with ``#include`` results in loading patterns from the "
"named file. It is an error for a file to not exist or be included more than "
"once. Note that while this can be used to include patterns from a file in a "
"subdirectory, the patterns themselves are still relative to the repository "
"*root*. Example: ``#include more-patterns.txt``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:62
msgid ""
"A pattern beginning with a ``!`` prefix negates the pattern: matching files "
"are *included* (that is, *not* ignored). This can be used to override more "
"general patterns that follow. Note that files in ignored directories can not "
"be re-included this way. This is due to the fact that Syncthing stops "
"scanning when it reaches an ignored directory, so doesn't know what files it "
"might contain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:69
msgid ""
"A pattern beginning with a ``(?i)`` prefix enables case-insensitive pattern "
"matching. ``(?i)test`` matches ``test``, ``TEST`` and ``tEsT``. The ``(?i)`` "
"prefix can be combined with other patterns, for example the pattern ``(?i)!"
"picture*.png`` indicates that ``Picture1.PNG`` should be synchronized. On "
"Mac OS and Windows, patterns are always case-insensitive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:75
msgid ""
"A pattern beginning with a ``(?d)`` prefix enables removal of these files if "
"they are preventing directory deletion. This prefix should be used by any OS "
"generated files which you are happy to be removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:79
msgid "A line beginning with ``//`` is a comment and has no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:81
msgid "Windows does not support escaping ``\\[foo - bar\\]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:85
msgid "Prefixes can be specified in any order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:88
msgid "Example"
msgstr "範例"

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:90
msgid "Given a directory layout::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:92
msgid ""
".DS_Store\n"
"foo\n"
"foofoo\n"
"bar/\n"
"    baz\n"
"    quux\n"
"    quuz\n"
"bar2/\n"
"    baz\n"
"    frobble\n"
"My Pictures/\n"
"    Img15.PNG"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:105
msgid "and an ``.stignore`` file with the contents::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:107
msgid ""
"!frobble\n"
"!quuz\n"
"foo\n"
"*2\n"
"qu*\n"
"(?i)my pictures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:114
msgid ""
"all files and directories called \"foo\", ending in a \"2\" or starting with "
"\"qu\" will be ignored. The end result becomes::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:117
msgid ""
"(?d).DS_Store # ignored, will be deleted if gets in the way of parent "
"directory removal\n"
"foo           # ignored, matches \"foo\"\n"
"foofoo        # synced, does not match \"foo\" but would match \"foo*\" or "
"\"*foo\"\n"
"bar/          # synced\n"
"    baz       # synced\n"
"    quux      # ignored, matches \"qu*\"\n"
"    quuz      # synced, matches \"qu*\" but is excluded by the preceding \"!"
"quuz\"\n"
"bar2/         # ignored, matched \"*2\"\n"
"    baz       # ignored, due to parent being ignored\n"
"    frobble   # ignored, due to parent being ignored; \"!frobble\" doesn't "
"help\n"
"My Pictures/  # ignored, matched case insensitive \"(?i)my pictures\" "
"pattern\n"
"    Img15.PNG # ignored, due to parent being ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:131
msgid ""
"Please note that directory patterns ending with a slash ``some/directory/`` "
"matches the content of the directory, but not the directory itself. If you "
"want the pattern to match the directory and its content, make sure it does "
"not have a ``/`` at the end of the pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:137
msgid "Effects on \"In Sync\" Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:139
msgid ""
"Currently the effects on who is in sync with what can be a bit confusing "
"when using ignore patterns. This should be cleared up in a future version..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:143
msgid ""
"Assume two nodes, Alice and Bob, where Alice has 100 files to share, but Bob "
"ignores 25 of these. From Alice's point of view Bob will become about 75% in "
"sync (the actual number depends on the sizes of the individual files) and "
"remain in \"Syncing\" state even though it is in fact not syncing anything (:"
"issue:`623`). From Bob's point of view, it's 100% up to date but will show "
"fewer files in both the local and global view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/ignoring.rst:151
msgid ""
"If Bob adds files that have already been synced to the ignore list, they "
"will remain in the \"global\" view but disappear from the \"local\" view. "
"The end result is more files in the global repository than in the local, but "
"still 100% in sync (:issue:`624`). From Alice's point of view, Bob will "
"remain 100% in sync until the next reconnect, because Bob has already "
"announced that he has the files that are now suddenly ignored."
msgstr ""
